From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:24:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 36/36] [AGS] Phase E: Engine/platform/dos/acpldos.cpp, the DOS
 platform driver

PATCH-SEQUENCE.md's own Phase E, written per its already-reviewed plan
(PLAN.md's 2026-09-10 review): AGSPlatformDriver::CreateDriver() had no
DOS branch at all -- every platform provides exactly one .cpp defining
this static factory method (see acpllnx.cpp/acplbsd.cpp's own identical
pattern), and DOS never did, so it was undefined at link time the
moment a full build finally got past every compile-time gap.

Extends AGSPlatformDriver directly, not AGSPlatformXDGUnix, per the
plan: the XDG unix layer's config/save directory search paths have no
DOS equivalent and aren't wanted here; AGSPlatformDriver's own base
defaults (every directory resolves to ".") already match this hub's
recommended DOS filesystem policy (confirmed during PLATFORM-SURFACE.md
research), so none of the five directory methods are overridden.
GetDiskFreeSpaceMB() uses DJGPP's statfs() (struct statfs's f_bsize/
f_bfree, both plain `long` under DJGPP's own <sys/vfs.h>, confirmed by
reading it directly) -- present and linkable per
tests/probes/djgpp-runtime/, but runtime correctness under DOSBox-X is
not yet verified (real hardware or an emulator run, not just a
build-host reproduction of statfs()'s own real behavior). CD player
methods are stubbed "no CD, always fail" per the plan and patch 0007's
own CMake-level Cda::Cda gate (never linked for DOS regardless).

Verified: the undefined AGSPlatformDriver::CreateDriver() reference is
gone, and this is the last blocker a full cmake --build build/ags
-j$(nproc) -- -k pass found -- ags.exe links clean. COMPILES reached.
